# Project Rules — Expense Tracker (Budget Envelope Edition)

## Stack
- Frontend: React + Vite, styled-components
- Backend: Node.js + Express
- ORM/DB: Prisma + SQLite
- Tests: Vitest (or Jest) + Supertest for API/integration tests

## Architecture
- Backend is the source of truth for all business rules. Never trust
  client-computed totals, balances, or budget checks — recompute server-side.
- REST API under /api. JSON in/out. No GraphQL.
- All money values stored as integers in the smallest currency unit (paise)
  to avoid floating point errors. Convert to display units only in the UI.

## The signature rule (do not simplify away)
A Category has a monthly budget limit. When a Transaction (expense) is
created, updated, backdated, or reassigned to a different category, the
backend must recompute that category's rolling total for the affected
month(s) and flag (not silently block, unless configured) whether the
category is now over budget. This must be correct for:
- backdated transactions (added with a past date)
- transactions moved between categories (both categories recalculate)
- transactions edited after creation (old month AND new month recalc if the
  date changes)
- the exact boundary (spending == limit is NOT over budget; only > limit is)

## Validation
- Reject on the backend: negative or zero amounts, missing description,
  invalid/nonexistent category, invalid date format.
- Return 4xx with a clear error message shape: { error: string, field?: string }

## Code style
- Functional React components, hooks only, no class components.
- Keep business logic (budget calculation, validation) in backend
  service/util files, not in route handlers directly — route handlers should
  stay thin and call into a service layer that's independently testable.
- Prefer small, named functions over large inline logic blocks.

## What NOT to do
- Do not add authentication — it's explicitly optional/out of scope for Core.
- Do not use localStorage/sessionStorage for persistence — must be a real
  DB via the backend.
- Do not invent extra entities beyond User (seeded), Category, Transaction
  unless I ask.

## AI workflow expectations
- When generating a new feature, first restate the plan in 2-4 bullets
  before writing code, so I can confirm direction.
- When touching the budget calculation logic, always explain the edge cases
  considered.
- Flag any assumption you make instead of silently picking one.
